WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:12.609
Life is a mess. There are all kinds of forms
of life on this planet, and any time you want

00:00:12.609 --> 00:00:18.570
to do anything scientific it’s good to have
some kind of organizing principle. Biologists

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:25.869
use a very rough organizing principle for
defining types of life by calling them ‘species.’

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:32.599
‘Species’ traditionally was the distinction
of different animals or different forms of

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:41.120
life which cannot interbreed or, even if they
do interbreed, their offspring cannot reproduce.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:47.870
This is a rough definition of course, but
it was useful in categorizing and enumerating

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:54.260
the number of types of of forms of life on
Earth there are. And now that that list is

00:00:54.260 --> 00:01:00.019
in the millions, we have a very complicated
web of what the tree of life looks like. But

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:06.500
even more interesting is that the ability
to access the genetic information of different

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:13.580
species had allowed biologists to see where
the lines are blurred between two different

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:21.300
types or more species. What they found was
interesting. First, that species — there

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:28.520
are many species which interbreed. They have
sex with each other, and they produce offspring

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:35.000
and a lot of genetic information is shared
between species. But what they’ve also found

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:41.130
is that there are genetic distinguishing features
that remain robust. It’s like if you have

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:45.180
two cans of paint and you pour them into each
other — say one yellow and one red — and

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:51.440
you mix it all up and it all turns orange
except for these spots. Some are exactly red

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.140
and the other ones are yellow and they don’t
blend for some reason — parts of the DNA

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:02.909
which stay robustly distinct between two species.
One example is in northern Europe there are

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:11.159
two different species of crows, the carrion
and the hooded crow. And yet they do interbreed,

00:02:11.159 --> 00:02:17.450
and they do live geographically in overlapping
places. And yet, their distinguishing features

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:24.209
remain. In fact, their genetic codes are so
similar that you, looking at the DNA, would

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:28.840
never call them different species, and yet
they look completely different and therefore

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:34.659
are easily distinguished. And the question
is: ‘Why?’ Why is it so robust? And we

00:02:34.659 --> 00:02:39.920
don’t know. And so studying the genomes
in great detail, of neighboring species and

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:45.249
lots of different species, we can understand
what we mean by the word ‘species’ at all.

